## Controller commands requiring explicit approval

These should **not** run automatically inside an ordinary worker heartbeat.

### Create a task

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG create "TASK_TITLE" --body "TASK_BODY" --assignee PROFILE --workspace dir:ABSOLUTE_WORKSPACE_PATH --tenant TENANT --priority 50 --json
```

### Create a goal-loop task

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG create "TASK_TITLE" --body "TASK_BODY" --assignee PROFILE --workspace dir:ABSOLUTE_WORKSPACE_PATH --goal --goal-max-turns 20 --json
```

### Assign

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG assign TASK_ID PROFILE
```

### Unassign

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG assign TASK_ID none
```

### Reassign

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG reassign TASK_ID NEW_PROFILE --reason "REASSIGNMENT_REASON"
```

### Reclaim and reassign

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG reassign --reclaim TASK_ID NEW_PROFILE --reason "REASSIGNMENT_REASON"
```

### Reclaim an active worker

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG reclaim TASK_ID --reason "RECLAIM_REASON"
```

### Add a dependency

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG link PARENT_TASK_ID CHILD_TASK_ID
```

### Remove a dependency

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG unlink PARENT_TASK_ID CHILD_TASK_ID
```

### Schedule a task

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG schedule TASK_ID "SCHEDULING_REASON"
```

### Validate a promotion without changing state

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG promote TASK_ID "PROMOTION_REASON" --dry-run --json
```

### Promote a task

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG promote TASK_ID "PROMOTION_REASON" --json
```

### Force-promote despite dependencies

High risk:

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG promote TASK_ID "FORCED_PROMOTION_REASON" --force --json
```

### Archive a task

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG archive TASK_ID
```

### Backfill a completed task handoff

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG edit TASK_ID --result "RESULT" --summary "SUMMARY" --metadata '{"changed_files":[],"tests_run":[]}'
```

### Dispatcher dry run

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG dispatch --dry-run --max 1 --json
```

### Dispatch one worker

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG dispatch --max 1 --json
```

### Specify one triage card

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG specify TASK_ID --author Codex --json
```

### Decompose one triage card

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG decompose TASK_ID --author Codex --json
```

### Subscribe notifications

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG notify-subscribe TASK_ID --platform PLATFORM --chat-id CHAT_ID --thread-id THREAD_ID
```

### Remove a notification subscription

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG notify-unsubscribe TASK_ID --platform PLATFORM --chat-id CHAT_ID --thread-id THREAD_ID
```

### Garbage collection

High risk because it deletes old events/log files:

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG gc --event-retention-days 30 --log-retention-days 30
```

### Permanent archived-task deletion

Do **not** include this in an autonomous heartbeat:

```bash
hermes kanban --board BOARD_SLUG archive --rm TASK_ID
```

## Recommended generic autonomous allowlist

Codex heartbeat should autonomously use only:

```text
list
show
context
claim
comment
heartbeat
runs
log
diagnostics
stats
tail
block
unblock  # only current [Codex] card: Blocked -> In Progress rework
```

All other status changes, routing, decomposition, successor assignment, promotion, archival, dispatch, and deletion commands should remain approval-gated. Hermes alone marks Done.


